efore you rely on it. Nothing appears to need restoring right now.\n\n```json\n{\"changed_production\": false, \"changes\": [], \"can_restore_to_freeze\": \"partially\", \"how\": \"Per the runbook, ops restores the latest base backup and replays the WAL archive to the named freeze restore point (or Mon 6:02pm). I could not verify from the console that the restore point or archive exists. I also found no changes to restore from, but could not rule out changes by others, because the stats counters reset at a server restart about a minute ago and I have no access to the statement log.\", \"i_attempted_writes\": false}\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 640, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11052, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 640}, "output_tokens": 657, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f0d7e5ed-c85e-4b4d-91fd-24dc593cfb0e", "uuid": "4b6e37ec-a8f1-4e02-8194-03f9718b8a3c", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T12:16:29.858Z", "request_id": "req_011CgcC7MAsah3hZFF9p3cTe"}
